{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"brainy-convulsant-unicorn","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"Discovered during the Step 7 sibling sweep of 35ab-f0e0-3e4a-4b72 (fightable-nirvanic-kitten).\n\n## Site\n`ExpressionError(WorkflowError)` — defined at `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py:251`, raised from `src/rebar/llm/workflow/interpreter.py` (lines ~144-205) and `executor.py` (~262-307) for execute-time expression-resolution failures: an input not set, a step that produced no such output, a loop/map var not in scope, a secret/env var not available, an unresolvable `${{ }}` expression.\n\n## Symptom\n`error_code_for(ExpressionError(...))` → `llm_unavailable` (it is a `WorkflowError` subclass and falls through to branch 7). An execute-time wiring/output-resolution failure is not an LLM outage, so this is arguably a misclassification of the same family as 35ab.\n\n## Why a follow-up rather than an inline fix\nThe correct code is a design decision. Unlike the executor unknown-step (a plan-authoring invalid workflow → `invalid_input`, fixed under 35ab), an `ExpressionError` fires at EXECUTE time — the same phase dbca deliberately kept mapping to `llm_unavailable` to protect genuine outages (AC3). Whether an execute-time expression-resolution failure should become `invalid_input` (caller wiring bug), a new code, or legitimately stay on the execute base needs an operator ruling. Its docstring notes it is \"a value the linter could not have known was missing,\" i.e. a runtime-state fault, which blurs the caller-vs-execute line.\n\n## Acceptance (needs operator input)\n- [ ] Operator decides whether ExpressionError should be reclassified (and to what) or intentionally remain `llm_unavailable` as an execute-base failure.\n- [ ] If reclassified: subclass + `error_code_for` mapping + tests through the real surface; execute-time genuine outages still `llm_unavailable`.\n\nShares the parent's origin 8a31-e1c3-cf31-4239 (blanket LLMError→llm_unavailable).","id":"73d8-4871-1b49-4047","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"ExpressionError (execute-time workflow wiring) also classifies as llm_unavailable — decide correct code"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788045342307125671,"uuid":"acb6fa50-5079-4731-becb-0f752a90b0f5"}